<BaseLayout title="The Car" description="1973 BMW 2002tii, chassis 2751676 — the car behind Voltii">
  <h1>The Car</h1>
  <p>
    A 1973 BMW 2002tii — chassis <strong>2751676</strong>, right-hand drive, delivered new
    with a factory-fitted Getrag 235/5 close-ratio dogleg 5-speed and a limited-slip
    differential, a combination fewer than 2,000 cars ever left the factory with.
  </p>
  <p>
    The plates read <strong>02TII</strong>. They stay. There'll be a cursive
    "Voltii" badge on the boot lid before this is done.
  </p>
  <p>
    This site tracks the conversion of that car to electric — a Nissan Leaf EM57
    motor, the original Getrag 245/4 gearbox retained via a BRAT Industries
    adapter, and the numbers-matching M10 engine preserved in storage rather than
    discarded. Read the <a href="/posts/introducing-voltii/">introduction</a> for
    the full story, or the <a href="/technical">technical page</a> for the
    current build spec.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
